  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "The eyelid noun עַפְעַף is covered in aphaph. Similar spellings for darkness and weariness have different senses and do not explain the flight in Psalm 18.\n\nAdded 2026-11-21: עַפְעַף, from its former one-word entry. Filed under the hollow root עוף: עַפְעַף is its reduplicated form, the eyelid as the \"flutterer\"; Ugaritic ʕpʕp keeps the doubled consonants and the sense.\n\nIts former note: The Ugaritic comparison preserves the repeated consonants and the anatomical sense. A further derivation from עוף “fly” on the basis of fluttering motion remains uncertain."
